🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- fixed-size arrays as struct fields, e.g.
🚽 `chad params[4];`. Exercises the core path: declare a struct with an
🚽 array field, read/write individual elements by index, and confirm the
🚽 layout (element size * count, correctly offset among the struct's
🚽 other fields) via maxxing().
gang Vec {
    chad params[4];
    rizz n;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Vec v;
    v.n = 42;
    v.params[0] = 1.5;
    v.params[1] = 2.5;
    v.params[2] = 3.5;
    v.params[3] = 4.5;
    yapping("%f %f %f %f %d", v.params[0], v.params[1], v.params[2],
           v.params[3], v.n);
    yapping("%lu", maxxing(v)); 🚽 4 floats (16) + 1 int (4) = 20
}
